From: airoha-port <airoha@local>
Subject: [PATCH] net: phylink: allow attaching a PHY for in-band 802.3z modes

5.4's phylink refuses to attach a PHY whenever the link is in-band and the
interface is 802.3z (1000BASE-X / 2500BASE-X).  That is wrong for boards
where the PHY sits behind the SerDes and only the *copper* side is driven
by the PHY: on the Nokia XG-040G-MF gdm3 is 2500base-x with an EN8811H on
phy-handle, and because phylink_of_phy_connect() returned 0 early the PHY
was never attached (pl->phydev == NULL, mac_link_up() receives phy=NULL),
so the EN8811H was never brought up and the port received no frames at
all while reporting carrier.

Newer kernels no longer carry this clause.  Drop it from both
phylink_attach_phy() and phylink_of_phy_connect().

Signed-off-by: airoha-port <airoha@local>
---
diff -ruN a/drivers/net/phy/phylink.c b/drivers/net/phy/phylink.c
--- a/drivers/net/phy/phylink.c	2026-10-10 18:34:59.105159871 +0800
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/phylink.c	2026-10-10 18:34:59.105159871 +0800
@@ -974,9 +974,14 @@
 static int phylink_attach_phy(struct phylink *pl, struct phy_device *phy,
 			      phy_interface_t interface)
 {
-	if (WARN_ON(pl->cfg_link_an_mode == MLO_AN_FIXED ||
-		    (pl->cfg_link_an_mode == MLO_AN_INBAND &&
-		     phy_interface_mode_is_8023z(interface))))
+	/* Only a fixed link genuinely has no PHY.  Refusing to attach a PHY
+	 * for an in-band 802.3z mode (1000BASE-X / 2500BASE-X) is wrong for
+	 * hardware such as the Nokia XG-040G-MF, where gdm3 is 2500base-x and
+	 * the EN8811H sits behind the SerDes: the PCS negotiates the SerDes
+	 * link while the PHY drives the copper side.  Newer kernels dropped
+	 * this clause.
+	 */
+	if (WARN_ON(pl->cfg_link_an_mode == MLO_AN_FIXED))
 		return -EINVAL;
 
 	if (pl->phydev)
@@ -1041,10 +1046,11 @@
 	struct phy_device *phy_dev;
 	int ret;
 
-	/* Fixed links and 802.3z are handled without needing a PHY */
-	if (pl->cfg_link_an_mode == MLO_AN_FIXED ||
-	    (pl->cfg_link_an_mode == MLO_AN_INBAND &&
-	     phy_interface_mode_is_8023z(pl->link_interface)))
+	/* Fixed links are handled without needing a PHY.  In-band 802.3z
+	 * modes may still have a PHY behind the SerDes (see
+	 * phylink_attach_phy()), so do not bail out for them here.
+	 */
+	if (pl->cfg_link_an_mode == MLO_AN_FIXED)
 		return 0;
 
 	phy_node = of_parse_phandle(dn, "phy-handle", 0);
